# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages types static files by extension, so /feed.xml went out as
# application/xml -- true, but not specific enough for a browser or a reader to
# recognise it as a subscribable feed. GitHub Pages had the same behaviour, so
# this is a long-standing defect being fixed at the migration, not a regression
# introduced by it.
# The CSP's real value here is the HOST ALLOWLIST: no external script origin
# can load unless it is named below, so any future third-party script is a
# visible diff rather than a silent addition. 'unsafe-inline' in script-src is
# load-bearing and an honest weakening -- the no-FOUC theme setter,
# CodeEnhancements, Mermaid, the Pagefind init and the analytics snippet are all
# inline, and nonces need per-request generation that a static Pages deploy
# cannot do. style-src 'unsafe-inline' is required by Shiki's inline style=
# attributes; frame-src covers the one youtube-nocookie embed in the corpus.
#
# cloudflareinsights.com is Cloudflare Web Analytics, and it is NOT in the build
# output -- Cloudflare injects the beacon into HTML at the edge, and only for
# requests that look like a browser. A plain `curl` never sees it, and neither
# does grepping dist/. The first version of this CSP therefore blocked it and
# broke a working analytics product that had been collecting for months.
#
# Two hosts are needed, not one: static.cloudflareinsights.com serves
# beacon.min.js, and the beacon POSTs its RUM payload to
# https://cloudflareinsights.com/cdn-cgi/rum. Allowing only the first would let
# the script load and then fail silently at report time.
#
# LESSON: verify this header with a browser User-Agent, not curl, and with
# DevTools open. Edge-injected scripts are invisible to every static check.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/feed.xml
  Content-Type: application/atom+xml; charset=utf-8

# Post source files (public/code/<year>/<month>/). Pages has no type for .pss
# and served them as application/octet-stream, so every "Raw Text" link
# downloaded instead of displaying. Everything under /code/ is plain text by
# convention -- keep binaries out of it.
/code/*
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
